;
CHAT WITH THE SYSOP

Type CHAT at the CP/M prompt to page the operator.
In RBBS, use C to return to CP/M first, then type CHAT.
Wait for the operator to answer. An unanswered page returns to CP/M.
Ctrl-C or Ctrl-X cancels the page or ends the conversation.

CHAT uses an 80x24 ANSI/VT100 split screen.
SYSOP types in the upper pane; CALLER types in the lower pane.
Each pane wraps and scrolls independently. Backspace erases text.
Ctrl-R redraws the screen. CHAT /S uses the plain scrolling display.
The sysop answers a page with Escape on the local keyboard.
Local Ctrl-G toggles BYE's page bell and paging availability.
Local Ctrl-B ends split chat and enters BYE's private-console mode.

For a message the sysop can read later, use MESSAGE or RBBS instead.
